# Codice Perfetto for Excubia App

`CLAUDE.md` and the issues of the current milestone are the source of truth. This rule does not add product scope.

## Ponytail

Pick the simplest solution that works. Stop at the first rung that holds: YAGNI, standard library, platform, installed dependency, one line, then the minimum code.

- No unrequested abstractions, dependencies, or boilerplate.
- Deletion over addition. Boring over clever. Fewest files possible.
- Mark an intentional shortcut with a `ponytail:` comment that names the ceiling and the upgrade path.
- Not lazy about trust-boundary validation, data-loss prevention, security, or anything explicitly requested.
- Non-trivial logic leaves one runnable check behind.

## Layers

- Never reimplement a check, parser, data-source client or renderer: they live in `qiick/excubia-core`.
- Thin controllers: validate with a `*Request`, call an `*Action` or `*Service`, return Inertia. No `DB` facade in controllers.
- `*Action` has one public `execute()` and handles writes. `*Service` handles reads, orchestration and integrations.
- Models hold relations, casts and scopes only. Authorization lives in Policies.

## Names

- Full words. No `cfg`, `res`, `req`, `val`, `ctx`, or `idx`.
- Loop indices `i`, `j`, and `k` only in tight numeric loops.
- Booleans and boolean methods use `is`, `has`, `can`, or `should`, except framework contracts and native React or DOM props.
- Only Eloquent models use bare nouns. Role suffixes match the architecture test: `Controller`, `Request`, `Action`, `Service`, `Data` (readonly), `Enum`, `Policy`, `Job`, `Command`, `Resource`, `Exception`.
- Starter-kit and `shadcn/ui` files keep upstream names.
- Frontend files are `kebab-case`; components and types `PascalCase`; hooks and functions `camelCase`.

## Documentation

- `declare(strict_types=1)` in every PHP file you write.
- English PHPDoc and JSDoc on classes, components, hooks and non-trivial methods: why, array shapes, side effects, and `@throws`. Not line-by-line noise.
- Explicit curly braces and a blank line around control-flow blocks.
- Do not leave `dd`, `dump`, `var_dump` or `console.log`. No `env()` outside `config/`.
- Migrations are forward-only: never edit or delete a merged migration.
